Discrete Elastic Rods (DER) — formulation attribution
-----------------------------------------------------
The elastic-rod losses in src/simplepredict/loss/ (der.py, bending_energy.py)
implement the Discrete Elastic Rods formulation of Bergou, Wardetzky, Robinson,
Audoly, and Grinspun, "Discrete elastic rods," ACM Transactions on Graphics
27(3), 2008 (doi:10.1145/1360612.1360662). This is an independent
reimplementation of that published formulation. Its structure was informed by
the reference implementation in roahmlab/DEFORM (Chen et al., "Differentiable
Discrete Elastic Rods for Real-Time Modeling of Deformable Linear Objects,"
CoRL 2024, arXiv:2406.05931); the Theseus-based twist optimizer from DEFORM is
deliberately NOT reproduced here (the twist angle is set to zero). roahmlab/
DEFORM publishes no license, so no DEFORM code is copied or redistributed; it is
credited here only as prior art that guided this independent implementation.


torchcurves — Apache-2.0, pip dependency
----------------------------------------
Differentiable B-spline curve fitting uses torchcurves (alexshtf/torchcurves),
licensed Apache-2.0, consumed as an ordinary PyPI dependency (torchcurves>=0.2.1)
and not redistributed in this repository. Apache-2.0 is compatible with MIT and
imposes no additional obligation on this repository beyond those already met by
declaring it as a dependency.
